    {
      "blocked_by": "the pinned PR386 sentence (windows sequential and immutable, per-call totals) and assemble.py's deficit literal; PR 2500: the typed contract alone does not imply fewer recursive children.",
      "content": "Admit one widened COPY/ERASE window with per-pair totals delivery (common sink) so the shared ledger n_8 = 576 / D = 9728 can be declared. Declared as an owner-ledger change only, the chain rejects it at the per-call profile/idle consistency (the rank-8 idle remainder goes negative: 576 - 1152); declared consistently per call (rank-8 children 8 -> 4), the chain rejects it at the SPEC pins expected.rank_mass / expected.profile and, with all pins relaxed, at assemble.py's literal owner deficit assertion. The chain moment oracle accepts the shared ledger at its own grid endpoint, but the chain's certify() search cannot reach it (bracket ceiling 0.003, engines/moment.py line 78; scoped obstruction recorded). Both are part of this decision.",
      "decision": "widened-window/common-sink contract change (vs PR 2500)",
      "id": "MD-1"
    },
    {
      "blocked_by": "the literal-window model (independent-t16: PASS_INDEPENDENT_T16_LITERAL_WINDOWS_CHARTS_PREFIX_ROW) and the 13-field provider local receipt schema.",
      "content": "Add declared fields for typed (frame-relabelled) window source rows, 8-row per-call windows and per-call totals delivery to the provider local receipt schema, plus their negative controls beside false_dirty_restoration in code/assembly_controls.py. Today no receipt field names a typed relabeling and any scalar re-window is rejected at the providers.<pid>.complete_contract pin (then the expected_local pins); a SPEC regeneration via the chain discovery path is the admission route.",
      "decision": "supplier admission fields for typed windows",
      "id": "MD-2"
    }
